// Supervisors on carriers (actor_memory_budget_plan.md item N, "Carriers are the only model"):
// 100 supervisors, each with one counter, under one root (its init lists 100 supervisor children,
// each started by sub_start, which picks the counter's id from the supervisor's initial state so
// every child id is distinct: spec section 20.3.1). Every supervisor is a carrier actor: no thread
// is made for any of them, so the process has as many threads as carriers, plus main (the
// thread-per-actor runtime made 100 supervisor threads and 100 worker threads here, and stopped at
// the per-task thread limit near 4,000 actors). What the program observes, deterministically at
// every carrier count and without reading the OS: the root counts 100 children; every child
// supervisor, reached by its id, is bound to a carrier (actor_carrier_index >= 0, which is -1
// only for a dangerous actor) and counts one child; and one counter answers.
//
// Expected output: 9 (the root counts 100), 9 (all 100 supervisors on carriers, each with one
// child), 505 (counter 7: 500 + 5), done, exit status 0.

use Supervisor;
use trial_wait_int64;

impl ZzsupManyRootSup for Supervisor;

